              "text": "The next NBA game is **Game 3 of the 2026 NBA Finals** between the **San Antonio Spurs** and the **New York Knicks**. \n\n* **Date & Time:** Monday, June 8, 2026, at 8:30 PM ET\n* **Location:** Madison Square Garden, New York, NY\n\nBecause the Knicks are currently leading the series 2\u20130 and hosting their first NBA Finals game in 27 years, ticket demand is historic, and prices are extraordinarily high (with resale \"get-in\" prices starting near $10,000). \n\nYou can find tickets for Game 3 (and subsequent games in the series) through the following platforms:\n\n### 1. Official Primary Seller\n* **Ticketmaster:** As the official ticketing partner of the NBA and Madison Square Garden, **[Ticketmaster](https://www.ticketmaster.com)** is the safest place to look for primary ticket releases and verified fan-to-fan resale tickets. \n\n### 2. Secondary Resale Marketplaces\nIf tickets are sold out on primary channels, you can purchase verified resale tickets on trusted secondary markets:\n* **TickPick:** Known for its \"no hidden fees\" pricing model. \n* **StubHub:** A widely used secondary market with a robust buyer guarantee.\n* **SeatGeek:** An official partner for many NBA ticketing platforms.\n* **Vivid Seats:** Another highly reliable alternative for secondary market tickets.\n\n---\n\n### Alternative Option: Official Watch Parties\nIf tickets to Madison Square Garden are out of your price range, you can still experience the game with fellow fans at official team-sponsored watch parties:\n* **For Knicks Fans (New York):** The Knicks are hosting an official **Game 3 Watch Party** at the Westchester County Center in White Plains, NY. Tickets for this event can be purchased on **Ticketmaster**.\n* **For Spurs Fans (San Antonio):** The Spurs are hosting an official **Game 3 Watch Party** at the Frost Bank Center. Tickets are available directly through the **Frost Bank Center website** or designated Spurs ticket outlets.",
